Use the real structured edit tool. Return ONLY JSON {"edits":[{"node":"an actual node ID from the source catalogue","changes":{}}]}. No fences or prose. One to sixteen node edits; every node ID appears at most once. No whole files or whole functions.
Upgrade span(a:u16,b:u16)->u32 to span(a:u32,b:u32)->u64, now returning the mathematical value a+3*b with complete u32 operands. Update entrypoint(a:u32,b:u32,c:u32)->u64 to call span once without narrowing and XOR its result with ((c AND 7)<<48). Replace both files atomically; the old coefficient and tag placement are obsolete.
The task's references to files mean their editable symbols; this interface accepts node edits only.
HIA replacements are instruction fields op/args/out/attrs, terminators, or explicitly enabled signature/block parameter types. Inserts use complete operation objects with op,args,out,attrs; delete is true by itself. All edits apply atomically and the complete program is reverified.
Public examples [arguments,[entrypoint,provider_probe]]: [[[0,1,1],[281474976710659,3]],[[65536,65537,4],[1125899907104771,262147]],[[4294967295,4294967295,7],[1970342016843772,17179869180]]]
